      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "My workaround for this is to swap the software buttons in my headset settings to different hands directly. However this causes issues with other VR games' bindings.\n\nFurther, it makes it so the Action Menu also opens in the other hand (because it believes it *is* the other hand), which is equally unusable for me. This makes me have to have an extra binding for \"Action Menu\" on my left hand.\n\nSomething that would be redundant if I could just change where the Quick Menu opens.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-10-07T09:14:54.650Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I believe this would make a great accessibility feature.\n\nAs it stands, the Quick Menu only opens on the same hand of the menu button pressed. SteamVR does not have separate bindings for left and right hand menus, Quest even less so. I would like the option to open the menu on the opposite hand as the button I press. \n\nThis is because I have a disability in my right hand that prevents me from using the face buttons on that controller, which makes my quick menu hard to access with my left hand as I cannot hit the right hand menu button easily to open it properly.\n\nThank you.",
